  "executable_evidence": [
    "Native PE64, XMRig 3.x-derived implementation; inspected XMRig v3.1.0 tagged source fetched with forager. This is source comparison, not a reproducible-build identity claim.",
    "Entry 0x14008ca64 reaches CRT main dispatch. Added main 0x1400e9e50 creates a named mutex. ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS takes a random sleep then return path; it is not a VM/sandbox probe.",
    "Main 0x1400e9f09 opens argv[0] in rb mode, seeks to EOF with 0x1400b3d88, obtains the length via 0x1400b357c, allocates a buffer and reads it through 0x1400b43c8 (fread). Calls and arguments were checked with Capstone after Rizin truncated some instruction windows.",
    "At 0x1400e9f74/78 it reads the final two dwords, decrements depth, and gates the copy loop on nonnegative resulting depth and positive fanout. Actual footer values are 540024856 and 540024880. These text-shaped values are interpreted as counters even though the appended data is malformed.",
    "At 0x1400e9faf the destination root is C:/Windows/System32/. Helper 0x1400ea8d0 selects random alphabet characters with rand()%52 and formats a .exe pathname. The returned path in RDI is both opened in wb mode and converted to the command line used by CreateProcessW at 0x1400ea0c0.",
    "0x1400e9fd0 copies image bytes minus 256+8 trailing bytes; the helper appends changing generated text, then two fwrite calls append the decremented depth and original fanout. All three fwrite calls resolve to 0x1400b3fe0. 0x1400ea0d9 branches back to the depth check; the output path remains the launched path.",
    "This routine precedes ordinary XMRig option/controller/miner initialization. Source comparison shows the mutex plus footer-driven clone loop is additional behavior, not the upstream App startup.",
    "Embedded JSON at 0x14012af20 enables cn/r CPU mining at 3.120.209.58:8080 with user/pass x, donation 0 and print-time 60000. Configuration loader 0x140004860 first tries command-line/config.json settings, then parses this embedded fallback at 0x140004a36 and passes it into Config::read.",
    "Stratum and CryptoNight/RandomX implementations match mining. GetConsoleWindow/ShowWindow(SW_HIDE)/FreeConsole paths remain guarded by the background config flag, which is false in the embedded JSON. LSA rights and token operations grant SeLockMemoryPrivilege for huge pages, matching upstream VirtualMemory_win.cpp. Neither establishes a UAC bypass, hostile console hiding or secret theft.",
    "Overlay starts at 1422336, containing a PNG, partial Pdfcrowd/Skia PDF and a very long random-letter suffix. All overlay MZ candidates fail PE signature validation; no embedded executable was recovered. 115 PDF Flate streams decompressed; they did not yield JavaScript/Launch actions. PDF annotations include an Apple-ID-shaped phishing URL and Pdfcrowd references, but no recovered code opens/displays this document. Treat the appended material as data, not an observed phishing stage.",
